  ('dd84ab07-01d4-4e28-a271-29243b1cc65e', 'fd0b2b54-7239-4012-acff-fec10dff456d', '2026-09-19'::date, E'lunch break entry.\n\ni cried in the car for no reason and then felt better. bodies are weird.\n\ni called my mom today and it was nice, we didn\'t fight about anything. i don\'t really know what i want right now and that scares me less than it used to. my sister is having a baby in december and i can\'t stop thinking about it.\n\ni said yes to something i wanted to say no to. again.\n\nspent way too long on my phone tonight. not great. therapy today. a lot came up. i\'m still sitting with it.\n\neveryone at work seems to have it figured out and i\'m just... here.', 'community', '2026-09-20T01:15:00+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-09-20T01:15:23+00:00'::timestamptz),
  ('2b1099e6-92d7-4008-8f21-676a89b966f7', 'fd0b2b54-7239-4012-acff-fec10dff456d', '2026-09-20'::date, E'honestly\n\n"when do you feel most like yourself?" — i don\'t know.\n\ni want to stop apologizing for taking up space. i finally finished that book. the ending wrecked me. there\'s this feeling where the afternoon stretches and nothing needs to happen. i want more of that.\n\ngot some good news today that i\'m not ready to share yet.\n\nthe dog woke me up at 5 and honestly the sunrise was worth it.\n\ni keep replaying a dumb thing i said in a meeting. nobody else remembers it, i\'m sure. i used to think being busy meant being important. work has been a lot lately and i don\'t think i\'ve admitted that to anyone. i keep starting things and not finishing them. maybe that\'s fine? maybe the starting is the point. the light in the kitchen at 4pm is my favourite thing about this apartment.\n\nbreakup stuff is still weird. some days fine, some days not.\n\nran into an old friend at the grocery store. we said we\'d get coffee. we won\'t.', 'community', '2026-09-21T01:24:00+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-09-21T01:24:32+00:00'::timestamptz),
